"""Human-reviewed source notes for remaining ten ACS records in B0009."""
import ledger as L
from review_batch_0001 import evidence
NOTES=[
('10.1021/acsphotonics.6b00062','SI pp2–3 FigS1–4','EDX and dark-field controls distinguish Ag/Au particles, ssDNA coating and subsequent assembly on an origami platform. This supports experimental origami use, but the inspected six-page supplement is primarily optical characterization/simulation, not a complete origami source set.','Acquire main design methods and parent platform; verify gap-setting and staple/capture variants.'),
('10.1021/acsami.6b04992','SI pp11–12 Methods2.1–2.3/FigS1–2; sequence-table headings pp3–10','M13mp18 rectangle approximately60x90nm has stated202staples and capture substitutions at named staple indices. Source says seven captures a1,b1,c1,d1,e1,g1,f1 but also six of which(b1to f1); repeated position44/36 and removal of24staples100–111/205–216 require reconciliation. Do not silently repair count/label inconsistencies. Particle release and logic states do not establish distinct scaffold cores.','Inspect FigS1 and full sequence/logic mapping; reconcile202staple count, removed strands and capture labels against parent rectangle.'),
('10.1021/acs.nanolett.6b03418','SI pp2–4 experimental section, pp5–8 assembly statistics and p9 sequence heading','Separately folded M13mp18 hexagonal tiles include core, functionalized edge and biotinylated staples. Dimers/trimers use distinct assembly annealing. i-motif and triplex connections respond to pH; T3/T7/T6 labels and T8/T9/T10 linear-to-bent assembly are kept distinct from core routing. Authors support intermolecular dissociation/recombination for isomerization.','Inspect complete staple/modified-strand lists and main diagrams; map tile variants and reversible connections. Preserve pH discrepancy in FigS3 recovery row versus Methods pending visual check.'),
('10.1021/acs.nanolett.6b03586','SI pp2–4 Methods, p9 FigS1 caption, pp23/37/50 table headings and p62references','Three cores explicitly described: twist-corrected24helix square-lattice rectangle90x65x2nm, hollow honeycomb tube83x23x29nm and compact honeycomb42HB60x26x16nm. p7560/p7249scaffold variants named but per-core assignment not established in inspected passages. 42HBhas21fluorescent sites using3prime22nt staple extensions and separate5primeAtto647N complementary strands. Magnesium/spermidine folding conditions are treatments, not new cores.','Inspect full CAD and all three staple tables, map scaffold per core and resolve parent refs1–3. Separate fluorescent adapters from core. No synthesis-set certification.'),
('10.1021/acs.langmuir.6b01961','SI all3pages text, especially FigS1','AFM caption directly documents AuNP-decorated origami nanotubes before and after metallization. NW1/NW2 are transport samples; no evidence here that they have distinct origami cores. Supplement focuses on metallization and conduction-model comparisons.','Acquire main nanotube preparation and parent design; determine scaffold, capture positions, lattice and complete sources.'),
('10.1021/acsnano.6b05276','SI pp2–3 FigS1–3 captions','Approximately47x44nm origami partially encloses two AuNPs; center is one layer. Orange attachment staples use3prime10A extensions, while up to four green staples carry5prime dyes. One-to-four dye loads are functionalization variants. TEM gap3.1plus/minus1.5nm is observed particle geometry, not a complete routing specification.','Inspect CAD image and main scaffold/staple methods; map dye/capture variants and parent platform.'),
('10.1021/acsami.6b10535','SI pp2–5 protein methods and FigS2–4','FigS2 explicitly shows Redbeta adsorption in holes of ordered origami masks. Other supplement sections concern protein purification and occupancy statistics; no new core can be inferred from different proteins or incubation conditions.','Acquire main mask design/assembly methods, parent source and staple set; verify exact mask versus higher-order array.'),
('10.1021/acs.nanolett.6b04146','SI pp2–4 folding/assembly/switching and map role caption; p7core table heading','M13mp18 cuboids distinguish body staples, polyT-passivated sides and left/right connector caps. Single/eight connector-pair and fully passivated variants exchange connector/passivation strands. Post-folding fibril assembly and thermal/chemical switching are separate operations. Body cites Nature Protocols9:1367–1391(2014); parent DOI pending. SI chemical-switching section states50mMconnector stock, unlike50micromolarfolding stocks; retain for verification.','Inspect full diagram/sequence list and identify parent protocol; reconcile connector-stock units with main/source context before reuse.'),
('10.1021/acs.nanolett.6b04169','SI p3FigS1caption, p4FigS2–3 and pp5–7TEM captions','Force-spectrometer CAD diagram labels nucleosome adapters protruding from top/bottom beams and fluorescent positions. Branched nucleosome template and four complementary handle sets are separate from origami core; expected10nm nucleosome attachment-site separation is not beam spacing. One/two-nucleosome conditions and salt titrations are loading/assay variants.','Inspect CAD image, remaining sequence sources and main methods; reconcile spectrometer parent and exact core variant before new-core counting.'),
('10.1021/acsami.6b10266','SI pp2–3 Methods2.1–2.3; p2 visually checked: group-count and repeated recipe wording confirmed','M13mp18frames combine G1(192),G2(16),G3(16),G4(16)helper groups; prose calls these three groups despite listing four. Frame1/3 both list G1G2G3 while frame2lists G1G2G4; actual distinct core count unresolved. C/Estrands added later. Separately folded DXtiles and protected aptamer-triggered interfaces are not additional origami cores.','Inspect complete group tables/diagrams and reconcile frame1/3identity; preserve three/four-group wording discrepancy and DXtile3mM stated concentration pending source check.')]

def main():
 pubs={p['registry_key']:p for p in L.read('publication_reviews')}
 for doi,loc,note,question in NOTES:
  p=pubs[doi];ev=[evidence(L.ROOT/'assets'/f['local_file'],f['url'],loc) for f in p['legacy_record']['downloaded_supplements']]
  p.update(review_stage='design_sources_reviewed',relevance='design_bearing',design_contributions=['uncertain'],catalog_eligibility='unresolved',access='partial',evidence=ev,rationale=note,unresolved_questions=[question,'Full design/source completeness and exact lattice eligibility remain unverified.'],reviewer='Codex named-section primary supplement inspection',run_id='B0009',date=L.DATE)
  L.upsert('publication_reviews',p,'Record supported use and inspectable source limitations, without counting assay conditions as new cores')
 b=next(b for b in L.read('batches') if b['batch_id']=='B0009');action='Reviewed remaining10ACS supplements at named sections; all15ACS selected records now inspected,20/25batch first passes total.'
 if action not in b['completed_actions']:b['completed_actions'].append(action)
 b.update(after_counts=L.counts(),validation=[L.validate()],unresolved_keys=b['input_keys'],next_queue=['Finish5remaining low/broad records:rsif.2012.0740,physreve.87.032702,pnas.1310092110,abstract144,andreconfigurabletubules.','Revisit explicitly recorded source contradictions and full sequence/CAD sets.','Continue FNANO2014 and backward/forward/author discovery.']);L.upsert('batches',b,'Checkpoint20/25first passes; remaining sources and discovery gaps explicit');print(L.validate())
if __name__=='__main__':main()
